# ============================================================================
#  Is this sender allowed to email the outside world?
# ============================================================================
#
#  Returns the string 'internal_only' for a mailbox that is NOT yet permitted
#  to send off-platform. Postfix treats that as the name of a restriction class
#  (defined in main.cf) which then permits our own domains and rejects
#  everything else.
#
#  Returns nothing for a sender that IS allowed — no row means no restriction,
#  and the rest of the normal checks apply.
#
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  WHY THIS EXISTS
#
#  Signup is self-service, so anyone can create an account. This is what stops
#  them using it to spam: until the tenant has verified a domain of its own,
#  its mailboxes can email their own organisation and nothing else.
#
#  It is the abuse control our Linode SMTP unblock request rests on. Removing
#  it does not just risk the IP's reputation — it makes the answer we gave them
#  untrue.
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#  Connects as tatvaos_mailedge: SELECT on routing tables and this view only.
#  It cannot read a single message.

hosts    = postgres
user     = tatvaos_mailedge
password = dev_mail_pw
dbname   = tatvaos_mail

# The decision lives in ONE place, mail.sender_gate_class() (migration
# 20261001-mail-sender-gate-bounce.sql), so this file and the database cannot
# disagree. It answers for a mailbox exactly as the query here used to, and
# ALSO for the send API's bounce addresses: until 1 Oct 2026 this file looked
# the envelope sender up among mailboxes only, a bounce address is not one,
# and so the send API's bounce-tracked mail passed this gate unchecked. A
# sender that is neither still returns nothing and falls through to the normal
# unknown-sender handling, as before. A bounce-shaped address with no send
# behind it is refused - see the function for why it fails closed.
#
# The mail edge has EXECUTE on that function and no grant on the tables it reads.
# tests/mail-api/test-bounce-gate.sh runs this exact query text.
query = SELECT c FROM (SELECT mail.sender_gate_class('%s') AS c) gate
        WHERE  c IS NOT NULL
